t_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting"}, {"defect": "There is no collar of brown or grey dead fronds under the living crown. The hanging fronds are the same grey-green as the live foliage (render-2).", "trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt"}, {"defect": "The trunk is a uniform dark mauve or purple-grey. The stub faces are no lighter or greyer than the shaft, so there is no weathered two-tone character (render-3 compared with reference-1 and reference-2).", "trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering"}], "observations": ["Four renders are included: seed 1 and seed 42 at P-WHOLE, plus seed 1 at P-TRUNK and P-BASE. The P-BASE input is marked visibility 'hidden', but the image clearly shows a close view of the trunk with pegs, and I assessed it as drawn.", "Both seeds match at the silhouette level: a single tall slender trunk, a compact radiating crown, and a flared base.", "fruit-clusters-pendent is a known gap (fn-111) and is not assessed. No fruit is drawn.", "The spruce anchor (anchor-0) was used only as the floor for finish quality. The render's finish is comparable, so finish is not what fails this candidate.", "Whether any change is a relative improvement does not decide readiness here. Several core traits and owner priorities still fail."], "findings": [{"observation": "Fronds radiate from a single apex, but most are held straight out or up as spokes. Only a few hang down beside the trunk, and there is no progressive recurving from young to old fronds. The crown outline is a spiky ball, not a hemisphere or shuttlecock. I estimate about 25–30 fronds are visible.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length and droop or curvature settings may be too low. This is not confirmed.", "trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds"}, {"observation": "Frond length is small compared with trunk height. Crown spread is about half the visible trunk length, whereas the fronds in reference-0 are long and heavy. The fronds also look sparse and thin, which matches the owner's complaint that they are 'far too thin and short'.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds"}, {"observation": "The leaflets are narrow and linear with sharp dark tips. They are inserted at differing angles and give a bristly margin, which is consistent with the reference character. Grouped insertion and a V-section cannot be confirmed at this resolution.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "render-1", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow"}, {"observation": "In both seeds the trunk has a distinct jog or elbow just below the crown. In seed 1 the lower trunk also has a slight S-curve. This breaks the owner's rule of straight or gently leaning and never wavy.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": null}, {"observation": "The trunk is single and unbranched, with roughly constant diameter up the shaft and a flare at the base.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem"}, {"observation": "Nothing grows on the trunk: there are no epiphytes or trunk foliage. Leaf-base pegs are the only protrusions, and the hanging fronds come from the crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": null}, {"observation": "The leaf-base stubs are widely spaced cylindrical pegs with rounded ends on a smooth shaft. They do not tessellate into a diamond lattice, and they have no flat, angular faces.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern"}, {"observation": "The trunk surface between the pegs is smooth and has no fibre or husk layer.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting"}, {"observation": "At close range (seed 1), the frond colour reads grey-green to blue-green with dark leaflet edges, which is consistent with reference-1. In the seed 42 whole view, the crown reads dark grey against the sky and dark leaflet tips dominate. With no close view for that seed, the hue is ambiguous.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-1", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "frond-colour-range"}, {"observation": "No dead or brown frond skirt appears under the crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt"}, {"observation": "The trunk is a uniform mauve or purple-grey-brown, and the stubs are the same colour as the shaft. At whole-tree scale (seed 42) the colour might pass as the uniform grey-brown seen in reference-0 at distance, but that cannot be confirmed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering"}, {"observation": "The trunk widens into a flared base where it meets the ground in both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "basal-flare"}, {"observation": "No smooth crownshaft is visible. The fronds attach directly at the top of the pegged trunk.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent"}, {"observation": "No fruit bunches are drawn. This is a known gap (fn-111) and is not assessed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent"}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The fronds radiate from the apex, but they are short, straight and held out like spokes. They do not arch into a hemisphere or shuttlecock outline, and few droop, so the defining arching crown character is missing."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "render-1", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The leaflets are narrow, pointed and set at varied angles, giving a bristly silhouette that matches the references. Their sparseness is a separate issue, recorded under frond length and fullness."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The stubs are sparse rounded cylindrical pegs. They do not form a dense diamond lattice of blunt, flat-faced wedges."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The trunk surface is smooth with no fibre between the stubs."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The stem is single and unbranched with near-constant diameter. The kink below the crown is recorded under the owner's trunk-straightness priority instead."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-8